From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:18:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: derive alpha to coverage without a colour
 attachment

Metal derives alpha to coverage from the alpha of colour attachment 0, so a
pipeline whose fragment shader Location 0 output reaches no attachment leaves
it nothing to read: a subpass with no colour attachment at all, or one whose
first attachment is VK_ATTACHMENT_UNUSED, where the Location 0 store is
dropped because Metal must not expose an output for an absent attachment.
Metal then rasterizes those draws fully covered, and Vulkan's rule that the
coverage follows the Location 0 alpha, gating the colour writes of the other
attachments and the depth and stencil writes of the subpass, is lost.

Compute the coverage in the fragment shader for exactly those pipelines and
turn Metal's own alpha to coverage off for them. The dither mask keeps the
number of set bits proportional to the alpha and produces one mask per alpha,
and its low 2, 4, 8 and 16 bits are each a valid mask, so a single value
serves every sample count. It is folded into the shader's sample mask output,
which Metal intersects with the rasterized coverage before the depth and
stencil tests. The lowering runs before the undeclared outputs are dropped, so
it still sees the alpha, and after sample shading lowering, so the coverage it
masks is already the sample being shaded.

Add a KosmicKrisp test that renders both shapes: a draw whose first colour
attachment is unused, read back from the attachment that is used, and a draw
with no colour attachment, read back through a second draw whose depth test
only passes where the first left the cleared depth.
